Task: MarkerAdapter.showIn optional; drop FIRE_FLAME.showIn (FR3)

Summary: Truthful marker adapter (the only red/green phase of the track).
The flame's visibility has always been owned by `fireFx` — `FIRE_FLAME.showIn`
was a describing field no production code read (a `markerVisible`-drives-flame
wiring would run `extinguish()` during the celebration and cut the lingering
smoke 2.5s early — a visible change rejected earlier). The contract now says
that out loud.

Red-then-green (vitest red run: exactly 4 failures, 17 passes):
- `MarkerAdapter.showIn` is now optional (`readonly showIn?: readonly S[]`);
  `markerVisible` treats absent as "drives no visibility" (false).
- `FIRE_FLAME` no longer carries `showIn`; its JSDoc names `fireFx` as the
  flame's owner.
- New tests: an adapter with no `showIn` is never visible through the generic
  sync while its `markerTap` seams still work; `'showIn' in FIRE_FLAME` is
  false (pin); every visibility-driving adapter (ORDER_CONE, PARK_FIELD,
  PUPPY_PAW, PUPPY_HEART) still declares its exact `showIn` states.

USER-SANCTIONED frozen-suite amendment (asked before implementation, per
workflow deviation protocol): FR3 contradicted AC4 because two assertions in
the frozen `missionMarkers.test.ts` pinned `markerVisible(FIRE_FLAME, ...)`
true in spawned/driving/active — the very field FR3 deletes. User chose
